development.solution_text:
In $\triangle ABM$ and $\triangle ACM$:
$AB = AC$ (given, isosceles triangle)
$BM = CM$ ($M$ is the midpoint of $BC$)
$AM$ is common.
$\therefore \triangle ABM \cong \triangle ACM$ (SSS)
$\therefore \angle AMB = \angle AMC$ (matching angles of congruent triangles)
$\angle AMB + \angle AMC = 180^{\circ}$ (angles on a straight line $BC$)
$\therefore \angle AMB = \angle AMC = 90^{\circ}$
So the line from the apex to the midpoint of the base is perpendicular to the base.
